      "Question": "Measure a spectrum 5 times at the same position and compute the sample relative standard deviation of the 1001 cm-1 peak intensity as a percentage.",
      "Ans": "### Experiment Report\n\n**1. Objective**\nThe objective of this experiment was to measure the Raman spectrum of a sample five times at a single position and compute the sample Relative Standard Deviation (RSD) of the peak intensity at $1001\\text{ cm}^{-1}$ to assess measurement precision.\n\n**2. Measurement Conditions**\n*   **Sample Position**: Identified via microscope image at pixel coordinates $(580, 670)$.\n*   **Focus**: Optimized using `run_autofocus`, resulting in a Z-position of $-0.0486\\text{ mm}$.\n*   **Laser Power**: $40\\%$ (chosen based on typical safe starting parameters for unknown plastics/polystyrene, as no specific protocol was found in the knowledge base).\n*   **Exposure Time**: $0.5\\text{ s}$.\n*   **Acquisition Mode**: Single shot, repeated 5 times at the same coordinate $(x=37.98, y=25.35)$.\n\n**3. Measurement Results**\nFive spectra were acquired successfully. The intensities extracted at the Raman shift closest to $1001\\text{ cm}^{-1}$ (actual shifted position: $1000.53\\text{ cm}^{-1}$) are as follows:\n*   Spectrum 1: $672.00$\n*   Spectrum 2: $681.00$\n*   Spectrum 3: $685.00$\n*   Spectrum 4: $689.00$\n*   Spectrum 5: $679.00$\n\n**4. Precision Analysis**\nThe statistical analysis of the peak intensity at $\\sim1001\\text{ cm}^{-1}$ yielded:\n*   **Mean Intensity**: $681.20$\n*   **Sample Standard Deviation**: $6.42$\n*   **Relative Standard Deviation (RSD)**: **$0.94\\%$**\n\n**5. Interpretation and Conclusion**\nThe calculated RSD of $0.94\\%$ is well below $1\\%$, indicating high shot-to-shot repeatability and excellent instrumental stability at the chosen power and exposure settings. This level of precision is typical for a stable Raman system and confirms that the measurement conditions were appropriate for this sample.\n\n**6. Problems Encountered**\nNo significant hardware or software problems were encountered during the process. The lack of a specific \"polystyrene\" protocol in the knowledge base was handled by using standard, conservative parameters ($40\\%$ power, $0.5\\text{ s}$ exposure) which proved effective and safe.",
